1
00:02:31,068 --> 00:02:41,068
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:41,068 --> 00:02:45,068
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:45,068 --> 00:02:52,068
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:52,068 --> 00:02:58,068
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the road, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:02:58,068 --> 00:03:09,068
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, set sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:09,068 --> 00:03:13,068
I will be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:16,068 --> 00:03:19,068
Two years have passed since the war in Marineford.

8
00:03:19,068 --> 00:03:25,068
Each of the Straw Hat Pirates underwent individual training and reunited at the Sabaody Archipelago,

9
00:03:25,068 --> 00:03:28,068
ready to take the next step into the New World.

10
00:03:31,068 --> 00:03:34,068
We're off to Fishman Island!

11
00:03:40,068 --> 00:03:44,068
Wait a sec. What is that thing? A fish? No.

12
00:03:44,068 --> 00:03:47,068
Are you ready? We only get one shot at this!

13
00:03:47,068 --> 00:03:49,068
Ready, brother!

14
00:03:49,068 --> 00:03:50,068
Ready, Captain!

15
00:03:50,068 --> 00:03:53,068
Before you say anything, I know what you're thinking.

16
00:03:53,068 --> 00:03:57,068
Hey, you guys! There's a ship-looking thing coming our way!

17
00:03:57,068 --> 00:03:59,068
Charge!

18
00:03:59,068 --> 00:04:05,068
It's a pirate ship!

19
00:04:05,068 --> 00:04:17,068
Deadly combat under the sea! The demon of the ocean strikes!

20
00:04:18,068 --> 00:04:20,068
Run!

21
00:04:21,068 --> 00:04:23,068
Hard support, now!

22
00:04:29,068 --> 00:04:31,068
Attack them, sea cow!

23
00:04:31,068 --> 00:04:35,068
They're tenacious, aren't they?

24
00:04:35,068 --> 00:04:36,068
That sound!

25
00:04:37,068 --> 00:04:38,068
They don't know when to quit!

26
00:04:40,068 --> 00:04:42,068
Who are these guys after?

27
00:04:47,068 --> 00:04:48,068
The bubble's about to pop!

28
00:04:49,068 --> 00:04:50,068
Keep it up, sea cow!

29
00:04:51,068 --> 00:04:52,068
Yeah!

30
00:04:52,068 --> 00:04:53,068
You think they want to board the ship?

31
00:04:53,068 --> 00:04:54,068
Sea cow?

32
00:04:55,068 --> 00:04:57,068
I know that noise from somewhere!

33
00:04:58,068 --> 00:05:01,068
The two bubbles are touching!

34
00:05:01,068 --> 00:05:03,068
This is a big moment, brother!

35
00:05:04,068 --> 00:05:05,068
Good!

36
00:05:06,068 --> 00:05:07,068
Is everybody ready?

37
00:05:08,068 --> 00:05:09,068
Yeah!

38
00:05:10,068 --> 00:05:11,068
Mumu, it's me!

39
00:05:11,068 --> 00:05:12,068
We've met before!

40
00:05:12,068 --> 00:05:13,068
You're from the Arlong Pirates, right?

41
00:05:14,068 --> 00:05:15,068
Do you remember me?

42
00:05:16,068 --> 00:05:17,068
Nami!

43
00:05:17,068 --> 00:05:18,068
I was at Arlong Park!

44
00:05:20,068 --> 00:05:23,068
Hey, Luffy, doesn't that thing look kind of familiar?

45
00:05:24,068 --> 00:05:25,068
I don't know.

46
00:05:25,068 --> 00:05:26,068
No!

47
00:05:29,068 --> 00:05:30,068
Gum gum pistol!

48
00:05:34,068 --> 00:05:36,068
Let's pay our new friends a visit, shall we?

49
00:05:37,068 --> 00:05:38,068
Yeah!

50
00:05:40,068 --> 00:05:41,068
Hey, that guy's up to something!

51
00:05:42,068 --> 00:05:43,068
Stay out of it!

52
00:05:44,068 --> 00:05:45,068
Guess he's looking for a fight, then!

53
00:05:48,068 --> 00:05:49,068
There's no time to waste!

54
00:05:50,068 --> 00:05:51,068
Follow my lead!

55
00:05:51,068 --> 00:05:52,068
No!

56
00:05:53,068 --> 00:05:54,068
Fools!

57
00:05:54,068 --> 00:05:55,068
They're completely dumbfounded!

58
00:05:56,068 --> 00:06:00,068
If they're gonna sit there catching flies, then we'll strike while the iron is hot!

59
00:06:01,068 --> 00:06:02,068
We'll smite this entire crew!

60
00:06:03,068 --> 00:06:04,068
Right now!

61
00:06:05,068 --> 00:06:06,068
For glory!

62
00:06:07,068 --> 00:06:08,068
Yeah!

63
00:06:09,068 --> 00:06:10,068
Come along, men!

64
00:06:11,068 --> 00:06:12,068
We'll make the beggars for mercy!

65
00:06:12,068 --> 00:06:13,068
What's wrong, Seacal?

66
00:06:13,068 --> 00:06:14,068
Don't panic!

67
00:06:14,068 --> 00:06:15,068
That's not good!

68
00:06:15,068 --> 00:06:16,068
We left Captain Terrible on the ship back there!

69
00:06:16,068 --> 00:06:17,068
Never!

70
00:06:18,068 --> 00:06:20,068
Now, it's time for a little greeting!

71
00:06:21,068 --> 00:06:22,068
Fire the Gatling gun, men!

72
00:06:23,068 --> 00:06:24,068
Shower them in bullets!

73
00:06:25,068 --> 00:06:26,068
I want every last one of them dead!

74
00:06:26,068 --> 00:06:27,068
Send these straw hats to hell!

75
00:06:27,068 --> 00:06:28,068
Huh?

76
00:06:28,068 --> 00:06:29,068
What?!

77
00:06:30,068 --> 00:06:31,068
Huh?

78
00:06:31,068 --> 00:06:32,068
What?!

79
00:06:33,068 --> 00:06:34,068
I don't know!

80
00:06:34,068 --> 00:06:35,068
It's time for a little greeting!

81
00:06:35,068 --> 00:06:36,068
Fire the Gatling gun, men!

82
00:06:36,068 --> 00:06:37,068
Shower them in bullets!

83
00:06:38,068 --> 00:06:40,068
I want every last one of them dead!

84
00:06:41,068 --> 00:06:43,068
Send these straw hats to hell!

85
00:06:53,068 --> 00:06:54,068
Huh?

86
00:06:57,068 --> 00:07:12,488
No! Wait! You're not going to throw me into the water, are you?

87
00:07:12,608 --> 00:07:14,988
Please don't do that to me, my friend! I'm begging you!

88
00:07:15,068 --> 00:07:17,388
Come on! You're a reasonable fellow, are you not?

89
00:07:18,008 --> 00:07:20,208
By the way, you're very good-looking!

90
00:07:20,708 --> 00:07:23,828
I'm sure someone like you understands the value of human life, right?

91
00:07:23,828 --> 00:07:28,468
And besides, the gods are watching! You'll be judged for this!

92
00:07:29,408 --> 00:07:31,568
Oh, make up your freaking mind already!

93
00:07:32,148 --> 00:07:35,868
Weren't you just about to fire your Gatling gun and blast us all to kingdom come?

94
00:07:36,108 --> 00:07:40,948
Me? No! I was just, uh, I was just joking around!

95
00:07:41,008 --> 00:07:41,828
I ain't laughing.

96
00:07:42,428 --> 00:07:46,908
Anyway, tell me. I know you're the captain of that ship, but what's your name?

97
00:07:47,348 --> 00:07:48,568
That's Roro no Zoro!

98
00:07:50,388 --> 00:07:53,688
Don't be ridiculous! What in the world makes you think I would be the captain?

99
00:07:53,828 --> 00:07:59,388
I'm, uh, oh! Those ruffians were keeping me as a, a slave! That's it!

100
00:07:59,808 --> 00:08:02,048
Boy! Ooh! Glad that's over!

101
00:08:02,648 --> 00:08:04,568
You know we're not buying this, right?

102
00:08:04,888 --> 00:08:09,428
Say, how's this? Do you think I could stay on this nice ship with you all for a little while?

103
00:08:10,008 --> 00:08:10,988
Huh? Please?

104
00:08:11,388 --> 00:08:14,408
Wow. I feel kind of sorry for this poor loser.

105
00:08:14,808 --> 00:08:16,948
He's obviously lying! Are you crazy?

106
00:08:17,448 --> 00:08:19,028
What? Seriously?

107
00:08:19,028 --> 00:08:23,848
Hey, I have a question. Where'd that giant sea cow pulling your ship come from?

108
00:08:24,268 --> 00:08:24,708
Hello?

109
00:08:27,248 --> 00:08:28,448
Oh my.

110
00:08:29,408 --> 00:08:30,808
Who's this vixen?

111
00:08:31,648 --> 00:08:34,108
I take it you're the famous cat burglar?

112
00:08:34,268 --> 00:08:38,848
Watch it, pal! Nobody's allowed to drool over our beautiful navigator except for me!

113
00:08:38,848 --> 00:08:42,608
Hey, don't worry. You're perfectly se...

114
00:08:42,608 --> 00:08:42,848
Oh!

115
00:08:43,268 --> 00:08:43,668
Oh!

116
00:08:44,408 --> 00:08:47,388
Hey, that's getting really old! Cut it out!

117
00:08:47,568 --> 00:08:51,768
The sea cow? Who knows? I just happened to catch it out in the ocean somewhere!

118
00:08:52,348 --> 00:08:57,708
When you're underwater, having a sea monster pull your ship is the mark of an experienced captain!

119
00:08:58,008 --> 00:08:58,288
Huh?

120
00:08:58,288 --> 00:08:58,588
Huh?

121
00:08:59,588 --> 00:09:00,128
Awesome!

122
00:09:00,128 --> 00:09:05,948
Stop it, sea cow! What's the problem?

123
00:09:06,248 --> 00:09:09,628
Brother! We're on our way to rescue you!

124
00:09:14,108 --> 00:09:16,488
I'm gonna find a sea monster, too!

125
00:09:17,428 --> 00:09:20,188
What crazy ideas are you hatching now, Luffy?

126
00:09:20,928 --> 00:09:22,248
Uh... Ooh!

127
00:09:22,628 --> 00:09:24,148
Hmm... Turtles?

128
00:09:24,728 --> 00:09:25,688
Ah, too small.

129
00:09:26,248 --> 00:09:26,928
Jeez.

130
00:09:26,928 --> 00:09:31,128
We should try to rehabilitate him with something a little less sexy.

131
00:09:31,748 --> 00:09:36,048
Hey, Nami, the direction we're taking isn't exactly the same way the log pose is pointing.

132
00:09:36,408 --> 00:09:41,928
Oh, no problem. The correct course is technically southwest, so we're in the clear.

133
00:09:42,048 --> 00:09:46,668
Yeah, but if we went in a straight line, we could get there a whole lot faster, couldn't we?

134
00:09:46,788 --> 00:09:49,968
Well, if you go straight, you risk getting swept away in a sea current.

135
00:09:49,968 --> 00:09:55,168
And if that should happen, you might run into an underwater mountain or a volcano, see? That's why.

136
00:09:55,168 --> 00:09:58,748
Huh? Yikes! I'm with you on this one!

137
00:09:58,928 --> 00:10:03,148
Yeah, but I thought all the currents here were dangerous. It is the Grand Line, after all.

138
00:10:03,488 --> 00:10:05,868
So are you saying that some of them are actually stable?

139
00:10:06,388 --> 00:10:07,528
Well, this one is.

140
00:10:08,188 --> 00:10:10,748
That should do it. Now you stay put.

141
00:10:10,948 --> 00:10:15,688
Hey! It's gonna start getting colder from here on out, so make sure you put on a coat or something!

142
00:10:15,688 --> 00:10:19,308
You bring up a good point. I'm already starting to feel goosebumps on my skin.

143
00:10:19,948 --> 00:10:21,928
Well, except for I...

144
00:10:21,928 --> 00:10:24,068
You don't have any skin because you're a skeleton.

145
00:10:26,948 --> 00:10:30,288
Chopper? Skull jokes are the only thing I have.

146
00:10:30,768 --> 00:10:32,308
Please don't take that away from me.

147
00:10:33,088 --> 00:10:35,748
We're going somewhere cold? Not the deep sea?

148
00:10:36,228 --> 00:10:38,768
Don't you guys know the water's cold in the deep sea?

149
00:10:39,168 --> 00:10:42,528
It's just like a bathtub. Hot water rises and cold sinks to the bottom.

150
00:10:43,288 --> 00:10:46,348
Oh, does it? I don't take very many baths.

151
00:10:46,408 --> 00:10:51,648
Aha! Because heat rises, and there's not much sunlight, so there's nothing to heat the water down here.

152
00:10:52,028 --> 00:10:54,948
The temperature's not the only thing that's different at the bottom.

153
00:10:55,528 --> 00:10:57,508
You're not still depressed, are you?

154
00:10:58,048 --> 00:11:01,748
Once we move down, we'll find something called deep currents.

155
00:11:01,748 --> 00:11:05,848
You don't run into them terribly often, but they're much larger than the regular currents.

156
00:11:05,848 --> 00:11:11,528
Also, they're quite unique in that their flow is completely independent of what you see closer to the surface.

157
00:11:12,048 --> 00:11:14,628
Currents? Under the currents? And you even have a diagram, huh?

158
00:11:14,868 --> 00:11:16,708
You sure do know a lot of stuff.

159
00:11:18,028 --> 00:11:19,728
That's because I'm so old.

160
00:11:19,988 --> 00:11:22,948
Not only that, but all currents are connected to each other.

161
00:11:23,428 --> 00:11:25,948
But that doesn't mean they have to flow in the same direction.

162
00:11:26,728 --> 00:11:28,928
They flow east, west, up, and down.

163
00:11:29,788 --> 00:11:32,448
It's like a big, long dragon, all tangled up.

164
00:11:32,448 --> 00:11:36,068
The deep currents tend to travel at a surprisingly slow pace.

165
00:11:36,508 --> 00:11:42,868
After they reach the deep sea, it takes approximately 2,000 years before they finally make their way up to the surface of the water.

166
00:11:43,248 --> 00:11:45,108
That makes me feel young again, actually.

167
00:11:45,888 --> 00:11:46,888
2,000?

168
00:11:47,688 --> 00:11:49,468
Yes, 2,000.

169
00:11:50,388 --> 00:11:55,768
And because of that, there are countless tales about what lurks within those deep, dark currents.

170
00:11:57,308 --> 00:11:58,868
Monsters. Curses.

171
00:11:58,868 --> 00:12:01,508
It's the wrath of the undead.

172
00:12:01,928 --> 00:12:04,648
You mean the deep sea is haunted?

173
00:12:05,008 --> 00:12:06,248
What? The sea's haunted?

174
00:12:06,768 --> 00:12:07,168
Help!

175
00:12:07,248 --> 00:12:08,648
That sounds fun to me!

176
00:12:08,788 --> 00:12:09,688
Calm down, guys.

177
00:12:10,228 --> 00:12:14,728
I don't know anything about the wrath of the undead, or whatever you're freaking out about,

178
00:12:14,828 --> 00:12:17,648
but I do know that we'll encounter a downward flowing current soon.

179
00:12:17,928 --> 00:12:21,508
Once we do, we should be able to ride it down into the deep sea.

180
00:12:22,468 --> 00:12:23,448
Deep sea.

181
00:12:24,288 --> 00:12:24,868
Surface.

182
00:12:24,868 --> 00:12:26,948
Lows downward.

183
00:12:28,008 --> 00:12:28,568
Flow.

184
00:12:28,868 --> 00:12:35,268
She said something about deep sea currents. I don't know.

185
00:12:35,388 --> 00:12:37,968
You morons can at least pretend like you understand me!

186
00:12:39,968 --> 00:12:41,788
Shall we sing a duet, Nami?

187
00:12:42,008 --> 00:12:42,628
Shut up!

188
00:12:51,928 --> 00:12:53,888
I hear something.

189
00:12:54,428 --> 00:12:55,208
It's here.

190
00:12:56,208 --> 00:12:57,468
Nami, I see it.

191
00:12:57,468 --> 00:12:58,428
Really?

192
00:12:59,208 --> 00:13:00,508
Shut it up!

193
00:13:02,968 --> 00:13:04,748
That's freaking sweet!

194
00:13:05,988 --> 00:13:06,568
Whoa!

195
00:13:06,568 --> 00:13:07,408
It's amazing.

196
00:13:07,768 --> 00:13:10,668
I admit, whatever that thing is, it's pretty cool.

197
00:13:11,168 --> 00:13:13,428
This one's called the downward plume.

198
00:13:15,928 --> 00:13:16,568
Whoa!

199
00:13:17,568 --> 00:13:19,928
It's almost like a giant waterfall!

200
00:13:19,928 --> 00:13:24,708
Except underwater!

201
00:13:24,708 --> 00:13:43,188
It's going so fast!

202
00:13:43,188 --> 00:13:48,888
The sea is, like, falling into the sea, which doesn't make sense, but I like it!

203
00:13:50,588 --> 00:13:53,008
Mother Nature, you're one crazy lady!

204
00:13:53,148 --> 00:13:54,808
What a spectacular sight.

205
00:13:55,288 --> 00:13:58,028
And from the looks of it, I'd say the stream runs fairly deep.

206
00:13:58,028 --> 00:14:02,268
I've heard stories about these currents, but they did not do them justice.

207
00:14:02,768 --> 00:14:04,448
It's crazy dark down there!

208
00:14:04,588 --> 00:14:06,708
The floor so far, you can't even see it!

209
00:14:06,748 --> 00:14:07,428
We're dead!

210
00:14:08,428 --> 00:14:11,308
At this speed, we're going to get pile-driven straight down to the bottom!

211
00:14:11,308 --> 00:14:16,688
You sure it's safe if we just go with the flow?

212
00:14:16,948 --> 00:14:18,928
If you're worried about the ship, don't be!

213
00:14:19,388 --> 00:14:21,568
Sunny was built from the treasure tree, Adam.

214
00:14:21,828 --> 00:14:23,188
It's as tough as they come!

215
00:14:24,048 --> 00:14:24,628
Okay!

216
00:14:26,388 --> 00:14:27,568
Let's go!

217
00:14:28,468 --> 00:14:28,908
Oh?

218
00:14:29,668 --> 00:14:31,068
Is that...

219
00:14:31,068 --> 00:14:31,488
Crap!

220
00:14:31,848 --> 00:14:33,808
So it really does live down here!

221
00:14:34,168 --> 00:14:35,048
It's no legend!

222
00:14:35,048 --> 00:14:49,548
A demon that rules over the deep seas!

223
00:14:49,908 --> 00:14:51,628
The enemy of all mankind!

224
00:14:51,628 --> 00:14:52,068
Night!

225
00:15:16,068 --> 00:15:18,088
Please listen to me, straw hats!

226
00:15:18,428 --> 00:15:20,168
We have to turn back!

227
00:15:20,168 --> 00:15:21,808
We're gonna die!

228
00:15:22,048 --> 00:15:23,728
Oh yeah, I forgot you were here.

229
00:15:23,808 --> 00:15:25,048
There's a sea monster!

230
00:15:26,648 --> 00:15:28,128
Cut it out already!

231
00:15:28,708 --> 00:15:29,688
There's no monster!

232
00:15:48,168 --> 00:15:49,588
They're just stories!

233
00:15:49,588 --> 00:15:51,948
Somebody made that up to scare people!

234
00:16:01,468 --> 00:16:01,828
Lisa!

235
00:16:02,188 --> 00:16:02,588
Jeez!

236
00:16:02,668 --> 00:16:04,068
What is the matter with you guys?

237
00:16:05,948 --> 00:16:06,428
Look!

238
00:16:06,548 --> 00:16:07,628
Just spit it out!

239
00:16:11,628 --> 00:16:12,548
Uh-oh!

240
00:16:12,548 --> 00:16:13,708
Okay!

241
00:16:13,788 --> 00:16:14,828
It's here!

242
00:16:21,888 --> 00:16:22,668
Okay!

243
00:16:22,668 --> 00:16:23,508
Hey?

244
00:16:23,508 --> 00:16:24,328
Waaaaa!

245
00:16:29,408 --> 00:16:31,328
It's the Kraken!

246
00:16:31,328 --> 00:16:32,168
No!

247
00:16:33,368 --> 00:16:36,708
Oh, legendary giant octopus monster!

248
00:16:36,708 --> 00:16:39,608
He made fish food out of those ships.

249
00:16:39,608 --> 00:16:42,928
They left for the new world and never made it.

250
00:16:42,928 --> 00:16:44,428
Turn around, please!

251
00:16:44,428 --> 00:16:45,928
I'm not ready to die!

252
00:16:45,928 --> 00:16:47,368
I beg you!

253
00:16:47,368 --> 00:16:49,508
Just wait around for a couple days

254
00:16:49,508 --> 00:16:51,408
and it'll probably go away!

255
00:16:51,408 --> 00:16:52,748
Shut up for a sec!

256
00:16:53,868 --> 00:16:55,908
I just had a perfect idea!

257
00:16:55,908 --> 00:16:57,008
Guys!

258
00:16:57,008 --> 00:16:59,048
We just have to capture it!

259
00:17:00,008 --> 00:17:00,848
Huh?

260
00:17:01,748 --> 00:17:04,008
Have you lost your mind, Loopy?

261
00:17:04,008 --> 00:17:05,048
Well, if we catch it,

262
